id: decisions/048-closed-status-field
title: "Close the status: field like epistemic_status"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'status-vocabulary-closure'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: status-vocabulary-closure
axis_gloss: "whether status values are drawn from a fixed enumerated set, or written freely per record"
poles:
  a: free-text-status
  b: closed-status-enum
split: lone-exception
draft_status: full
leverage: 3.4
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(7) x split_weight(0.4) x authored_conflict_bonus(1.2)"

question: >
  Should the top-level status: field draw from a closed list, as
  epistemic_status now does under a test, or stay free text that each file
  coins?

why_it_matters: >
  The repo already ruled, with a test and a shrinking grandfather ledger, that
  free-text epistemic statuses make records uncomputable, yet the top-level
  status: field carries 38 distinct values across 176 files, and one ledger
  violates the enum it declares two lines above its own entry. Once answered, a
  bot that ranks or graduates records can compute over status:, and a child Yawn
  inherits a lifecycle vocabulary instead of a folder habit.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    6 judgments sit at free-text-status (0 authored) and 1 at closed-status-enum
    (1 authored). The repository asserts both directions on this axis.
  attributed_to: TAXONOMY.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    What Dave wants status: to mean, lifecycle, maturity or workflow, since the 38
    current values mix all three; and whether schemas/statuses.v1.schema.json,
    unused by any record, is to be adopted or retired.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: status: is free text. Each folder may coin its own values. The
      closed-enum rule applies to epistemic_status only.
    cost: "None now; schemas/statuses.v1.schema.json lifecycleStatus stays unused."
    risk: "The rationale the repo wrote for closing epistemic_status ('no ranker, graduation ladder, or claim calculator can operate over an open vocabulary') applies word for word to status: and is left unanswered."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "None can enforce this; the record would be a note that status: is not machine-read."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0043"
      - "J0247"
      - "J0386"
      - "J0628"
      - "J0713"
      - "J0767"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: status: holds exactly one value from a closed set (the lifecycleStatus
      five in schemas/statuses.v1.schema.json: draft, active, superseded, archived,
      deleted, or the set Dave names). Maturity and version markers (v0-seed,
      draft-0.2, v1) move to a separate version: or maturity: key. The 38 legacy
      values are grandfathered by file in a test and the list may only shrink. A
      file that declares its own entry enum must satisfy it.
    cost: "A test modelled on tests/epistemic-status-vocabulary.test.mjs with a 38-value grandfather map; new records use the enum; records/yawn.bot-private-pr-ledger.yawn entry fixed."
    risk: "The five lifecycle values do not cover workflow states the repo uses (owner-review-required, waiting, proposed), so authors invent qualifiers elsewhere."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "tests/status-vocabulary.test.mjs: CANONICAL set, frozen GRANDFATHERED map keyed by file, may only shrink; plus a check that a file declaring an entry_shape enum has entries inside it."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0592"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: status: is closed in the machine-read roots (core/, agents/,
      automation/, records/, schemas/, templates/) and free in examples/ and
      references/. The closed set and the grandfather ledger are as in B.
    cost: "As B, minus examples/ and references/."
    risk: "Two regimes for one key; a bot must know the folder before reading the field."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "As B with a folder allowlist in the test."
    evidence_for:
      - "J0592"
      - "J0386"
      - "J0713"

recommendation:
  option_ref: B
  confidence: 0.7
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    By count this is six revealed against one, but the one is the only authored
    judgment, it is proof-attached (tests/epistemic-status-vocabulary.test.mjs,
    GROUND_TRUTH FACT 7), and its stated rationale is general, not specific to
    epistemic_status. The six free-text judgments are all revealed practice with
    no reason given anywhere. J0628 shows that even a self-declared enum is broken
    without a test. The enforcement mechanism already exists and works; B
    transplants it. The 38 values (FACT 2) mix lifecycle, maturity and workflow,
    so the enum design is the open question, and that is Dave's.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "One record names the closed set for status: and says where maturity and version markers go."
    - "A test in tests/ rejects status: values outside the set, holds a frozen grandfather map that may only shrink, and passes."
    - "records/yawn.bot-private-pr-ledger.yawn's entry matches its own entry_shape enum."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    The test lands but the grandfather map grows on the next pull request.
  status: proposed

evidence_sample:
  - "J0043"
  - "J0247"
  - "J0386"
  - "J0628"
  - "J0713"
  - "J0767"
  - "J0592"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
  id_index: TAXONOMY.md
